Not sure where this is coming from, sharing the same async websession or something else.
The code from the garmin_connect.zip code above worked fine for two accounts right?

I can reproduce it now using just the python-garminconnect-ha code example.
It seems User-Agent related, so I must have forgot one somewhere or HA is overruling it anyway.

In python-garminconnect-ha/garminconnect/--init--.py the definition of headers:

```
        # works:
        headers = {
             "User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Ubuntu; Linux x86_64;"
             " rv:48.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/50.0"\
         }


        # gives 403 on login(), the error preventing to init integration:
        headers = {
           "User-Agent": "HomeAssistant/2021.6.5 aiohttp/3.7.4.post0 Python/3.9.4"
        }
        # gives 403 on login(), the error preventing to init integration:
        headers = {
           "User-Agent": "Python/3.9.4"
        }

        # works:
        headers = {
           "User-Agent": "Blabla"
        }
````

So Garmin/Cloudflare is blocking certain keywords, like 'Python'??? Or coincidence? (I tried them 10+ times)

Correct, this one works as well:

```
        headers = {
           "User-Agent": "HomeAssistant/2021.6.5 aiohttp/3.7.4.post0"
        }
```

